tests/python-deps.bats
# runs 31877495900 … 31904202657: notok=3 on TWELVE consecutive runs — the only suite red in every
# one of them, so this single entry is what has stood between the producer and a green all day.
# MEASURED, not a hint, and the cause is named: the lint asks whether a bare command name resolves
# on the PATH a launchd job or hook actually runs under, and the answer is a fact about WHICH
# BINARIES THE MACHINE HAS. The runner image ships none of tmux, kitty, pnpm, yarn, uv; the box the
# daemons run on resolves all five inside the hardened PATH itself (/opt/homebrew/bin ×4,
# /usr/local/bin/yarn), which is why it is 18/18 green here and 15-ok/3-notok there. An off-box
# verdict on this suite is a claim about the runner's package set, never about our tree.
# ⚠️ 2026-08-23: this comment used to close by citing its sibling tests/unattended-sysctl-path.bats
# as excluded "for this class". That is no longer true, and the reason it was ever cited was wrong.
# The sibling was never machine-coupled — its notok=2 was an inverted test (see its DELIST note
# above), which is why fixing the test alone cured it off-box while THIS entry, which really is a
# claim about the runner's package set, is untouched. Two entries can share a seed run without
# sharing a cause; only this one has the cause named.
tests/unattended-path-lint.bats
