# 2026-08-13: tests/tsv-field-collapse.bats REMOVED — the first entry this list has ever shed, and
# the shrink arm named it rather than a human noticing. Its run-31369960469 measurement was notok=1
# on case 25 (an unpadded TSV reader in bin/cc-offload), which has since been fixed; case 34 then
# broke for an unrelated reason (0x1f is the gzip magic, so a vendored .gz fixture matched) and that
# is fixed too. Re-measured through the producer's own runner: green, 34/34. Both recorded causes
# are gone, so the line had lost its reason — and an exclusion nothing re-tests is a permanent hole,
# which is exactly what this file's own header says the census arm exists to prevent.
# run 31369960469: CUT at the 120s bound — a non-verdict, not a red. Excluded on COST, like
# postland-verify.bats below, and re-admissible if it ever gets faster.
# ⚠ RE-MEASURED AND KEPT (2026-08-21). It is green in all three censuses — 53/53 at 252s, 249s and
# 251s — but it did not get faster; the BOUND got bigger (120 → 300, and that raise was decided on a
# different suite's numbers). 251 of 300 is 84% of the budget, which puts this suite inside the tail
# of the distribution its own bound is drawn from — the exact condition hermetic.yml's bound comment
# names as unable to discriminate a hung suite from a slow one. Admitting it would make the producer
# a coin-flip on every slow runner, and the cost of THAT direction is the one this file's header
# calls unrecoverable: an over-broad entry loses coverage that never existed, a wrong deletion stops
# the producer producing anything for everyone. The entry's own condition is still the right one —
# delete it when the SUITE gets faster, not when the bound moves.
tests/worktree-gc-infra.bats

# ── 2026-08-21: TEN ENTRIES DELISTED — the shrink half fired for the first time at scale ─────────
# backlog e15a743e12ba. Read together with the FOURTH SEEDING block this replaces, because that
# block is the one that wrote its own release condition and then waited eleven days for someone to
# read it: *"The entry stays until a census MEASURES it surviving … Run the census, and if this
# suite comes back green, delete these three lines."* Nothing was wrong with the machinery. The
# daily census had been running since 2026-08-12 and its verdict job had been printing
# `release candidates (16)` into a step summary nobody opened. A detector with no reader is the same
# artifact as a detector with no owner.
#
# THE BAR APPLIED HERE IS STRICTER THAN THE ONE THIS FILE ASKS FOR, deliberately. The header says
# "Run the census, confirm the suite is green off-box, delete its line". One run is one sample, and
# the direction of a wrong deletion is the expensive one — an over-broad entry loses coverage that
# never existed, a wrong deletion stops the producer producing anything for everyone. So each line
# below is green in THREE independent censuses (32124683059 · 32240707543 · 32357106290, the daily
# `43 9 * * *` runs of 2026-08-18/19/20, 510/515/517 suites executed), at its FULL test count in the
# revision each run actually saw, with its recorded cause named as dissolved. Six of the sixteen
# candidates were withheld on that bar and each carries its reason at its own line above.
#
#   tests/land-gate-cas.bats            15/15 · 78s/61s/61s — green, and the DELETION STANDS: the
#     three-census bar was met. But the CAUSE recorded here was wrong, and is corrected 2026-08-21
#     (recycle #127, backlog 4eafdbe0a072). It read: *"its entry's own hypothesis (a bound sized on
#     a fast box truncating on a slow one) is consistent with the cure: the per-suite bound went
#     120 → 300 in hermetic.yml."* Three measurements refute that:
#       · The 120 → 300 raise is real, but it landed at 33a8f41a8, 2026-08-12T09:36Z — BEFORE all
#         three cited reds (bc8327717 22:01 · aee9071d7 23:56 · e71ea0b66 2026-08-13T01:23). Read
#         the value out of each of those trees: all three already say '300'. A change that precedes
#         every failure it is credited with curing cannot be its cure.
#       · Those runs took 40s / 43s / 51s — 13-17% of that bound. None was ever CUT; all three fold
#         `red ok=14 notok=1` at the SUITE level. (Run 31657575571's JOB verdict does read "cut",
#         because 42 OTHER suites went unreported. That is a different fact about a different
#         population, and it is the easiest one to read onto this row by mistake.)
#       · The three reds are TWO causes, not one. bc8327717 and aee9071d7 predate c5f1d1d56 and are
#         the stale-WORDING red it fixed. e71ea0b66 carries c5f1d1d56 AND a2de71b95 and is the
#         stale-MODE red: a2de71b95 made ship-land run the sweep `--mine`, so the fixture's 40
#         strands belong to no session, the sweep correctly reports CLEAN, and the un-mine verdict
#         the case grepped out of `$output` became unreachable. Cured by 565606e1e (2026-08-15) —
#         which is what the suite's own header at the "many refs" case already documents.
#     A/B on this desk, plain env, scratch trees: pre-fix sha e71ea0b66 reds ON-BOX (notok=1, at the
#     `on 40 of 6[0-9][0-9] local branch(es)` grep), HEAD is green, prior-shape control asserted in
#     both directions. So the entry's "red off-box only / green on-box" framing was false at its own
#     sha as well: the defect was deterministic, and the on-box corpus could always have seen it.
#     KEPT RATHER THAN DELETED because the wrong cause is the reusable part. Three genuinely green
#     censuses corroborated a mechanism that never operated — and a true metric beside a false cause
#     reads as diagnosed (memory: wrong-cause-corroborated-by-true-metric). The next reader of a
#     land-gate-cas red would have gone to the bound. The real mechanism is a semantic conflict
#     between sibling lands 19 minutes apart, neither an ancestor of the other, which no clean
#     rebase can see — a class that recurs, and one a timing hypothesis will never surface.
#   tests/iterm-sticky-command.bats      7/7 · ~1s — no `skip` in the file; the terminal-emulator
#   tests/kitty-recovery-launch.bats   19/19 · ~13s — class header's HINT ("a hosted runner has no
#     terminal application") turns out not to bind these two: they assert text, not a live emulator.
#   tests/capacity-ramp.bats           20/20 · ~8s — the launchd/QoS HINT does not bind it either.
#   tests/task-quality-gate.bats       10/10 · ~3s
#   tests/handoff-fired-cwd-index.bats 19/19 · ~4s
#   tests/bats-assert-liveness.bats    36/36 · ~15s
#   tests/session-end-gc-lock.bats       7/7 · ~15s
#   tests/live-session-registry-atomic.bats  8/8 then 15/15 · ~6s — bdf57e195 grew it mid-window;
#     green at full count on both sides of that commit, which is a stronger result than either alone.
#   tests/pkill-scope.bats             22/22 · ~11s — THE NAMED ONE. Its exclusion was never about
#     the suite failing; the suite passed and then SIGTERMed the shard, losing the 34 suites behind
#     it. ed095d4be gave the runner `trap '' TERM` so a process-killing suite costs its own row and
#     nothing else. Three censuses ran it green with the shard intact, which is the measurement its
#     own entry demanded before the fix could be believed.

