# ── 2026-09-05: FIFTH SEEDING — and the triage says the LIST IS NOT THE BLOCKER ──────────────────
# backlog 8fd1919f7769 ("T1H can never fire … triage per suite: machine-coupled vs genuinely
# broken"). Every entry below carries TWO measurements, not one, because a single off-box red cannot
# tell the two classes apart and this file's whole contract is that an entry is a measurement:
#   (1) OFF-BOX, four consecutive folds — runs 33883119356 · 33921137472 · 33931675582 ·
#       33944444105 (2026-09-04T14:20Z → 2026-09-05T04:24Z, 537-541 suites each).
#   (2) ON THIS BOX, through the producer's OWN runner and therefore the producer's own environment
#       axes (`scripts/offbox-run.sh suites <paths>`: empty $HOME, env -i, LC_ALL=C, TERM=dumb).
#       That is the discriminator the admission lint's header names — it reproduces the ENVIRONMENT
#       axes and not the MACHINE axes, so a suite that is red off-box and GREEN here has failed on
#       an axis the runner has and this desk does not.
#
# 🚨 THE RESULT MATTERS MORE THAN THE FOUR ENTRIES, AND IT CONTRADICTS THE ROW THAT ASKED FOR THEM.
# Nine suites were red in run 33944444105. Under (2), FIVE of them are red HERE too, deterministically
# — typed-send-lint (3), validate-bash-differential (6), goal-inert-watch (1), bash-audit-attrib (3),
# deploy-link-parity (2). They are not machine-coupled and they do not belong in this file; they are
# real defects in the tree, and the reason nobody is looking at them is that the ON-BOX corpus (T1)
# is starved, not that the off-box one is noisy. So adding the four lines below takes the fold from
# 9 red + 1 non-verdict to 5 red, and T1H STILL cannot fire. Excluding the rest would be curating a
# green, which is the one thing this file's header forbids. The remaining five are recorded, with
# their reproductions, in docs/research/offbox-red-triage-2026-09-05.md.
#
# NOT ADDED, deliberately: tests/live-session-registry-atomic.bats — red in 2 of the 4 folds and
# GREEN here at 15/15. It was DELISTED 2026-08-21 against a three-census bar; re-admitting a suite
# on a 2-of-4 flake would undo that on weaker evidence than removed it. Its off-box failure emits
# `not ok 8` and then `ok 8` with "Executed 16 instead of expected 15" — a bats job-control artifact
# at `sleep 30 & … kill … wait`, not a claim about the code. Re-check it on a census, not on a fold.

# HINT (not verified): reso-resume-one's argv layout is asserted against a live fleet's binaries.
