tests/cc-resume-field-order.bats
# MEASURED, and the cause is NAMED — this is not a hint. off-box red 4/4 (notok=1, case 26); on this
# box GREEN 27/27 in 101s. The failing case asserts its inline defect prints exactly `FALSE`, and the
# runner's output is `cat: stdout: Broken pipe` then `FALSE`: GNU coreutils' cat DIAGNOSES EPIPE on
# stderr, BSD cat is silent. The verdict off-box is a claim about which cat the image ships, never
# about our tree. Cure (a) — teach the case to tolerate the diagnostic — is preferred and is why this
# entry names the mechanism rather than a hint: it is one line away from deletable.
tests/pipefail-sigpipe-lint.bats
# HINT (not verified): CF1/CF2/CF3/CF5 assert a Darwin coalition footprint reads `measured` and that
# the per-process footprint parses as a number — the same machine surface its already-excluded
# siblings capacity-alarm-launchd-path.bats and capacity-admit.bats sit here for.
# off-box red 4/4 (notok=4). ⚠ THE LOCAL LEG IS A CUT, NOT A GREEN: on this box it reached 28 ok / 0
# notok and was CUT at the 300s bound, so measurement (2) ABSTAINS here and the class placement is
# the argument. Stated rather than rounded up, because a cut is not a green (offbox-run.sh R6).
tests/capacity-alarm.bats
# NON-VERDICT 4/4, never a red — it named zero failing tests in any of the four folds. Its TAP body
# ends `bats: … Terminated: 15 | bats_test_count_validator` after ok 194: the suite SIGTERMs the
# harness running it. That is the tests/pkill-scope.bats shape exactly (excluded, then cured by
# ed095d4be giving the runner `trap '' TERM`, then delisted 2026-08-21), and it is excluded on the
# same ground postland-verify.bats is: a suite that cannot produce a verdict cannot be part of a
# per-commit second opinion. Delete this line when its own TAP body completes off-box.
tests/cc-reaper.bats
